messages:
alex: Quick check — adding a tiny logging middleware to staging to help debug failing reroutes. Should we strip Authorization + any prompt fields in the request body? snippet below.

alex: ```js
// middleware
app.use((req,res,next) => {
  console.log('req headers', req.headers);
  console.log('req body', req.body);
  next();
});
```

mira: Short answer: yes redact Authorization header always. No raw prompts in logs unless hashed/pseudonymized and approved.

sam: For hash approach, ok to HMAC the prompt with a per-team key? We need it searchable.

mira: HMAC is fine for staging for short-term debug. Make sure keys live in KMS and rotate. Store only the hash, not the raw text. Add TTL for those entries.

alex: Also streaming responses — we log partial chunks by mistake. Should we stop logging response bodies entirely?

mira: Don't log streaming tokens. Log only high-level metadata (status, latency, final token count). If you must capture a snippet, capture a 50-char prefix after HMACing or with redaction.

deploy-bot: deploy scheduled: staging/services/edge: 2026-03-18T14:22Z

nate: Approve short-term staging capture with these controls: header strip, prompt HMAC, KMS keys, 72h retention, audit tag. For prod — open a ticket with justification + customer data risk review.

alex: Thanks. I'll push a config PR and add a Jira link in the PR description.

sam: PR please tag @mira and @nate so we can fast-track review :thumbsup:

mira: Also add a note in the runbook about how to revoke HMAC key in emergencies.

alex: Will do. Closing this thread after PR created.
